WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.810
Kotoko-san.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.300
What is it?

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.410
Can you hold my hand during the surgery?

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.320
Good luck, Non... Nobuhiro-kun.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.490
Non-chan is fine.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.620
Non-chan, you’re just too cute!

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.390
What’s wrong with you? How creepy.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.280
Aww, don’t be shy.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.670
I got an idea. Why don’t I hold your hand again?

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.950
Just like during the surgery.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.340
Ah, that?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.140
I only said that because I didn’t want you to do anything during the surgery.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.790
Yuuki-kun?

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.540
Oh, you came to see me?

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.750
How are you feeling?

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.400
Not too well.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.030
But, Kotoko-san told me to leave the hospital.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.140
What are you saying? Your post-operative progress is excellent, right?

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.620
That’s good.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.070
That’s right. Your fans are waiting for you to return, right?

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.660
But, I don’t want to be separated from you.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.070
But, I have a wonderful husband named Irie-kun.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.870
Don’t take him seriously.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.720
You really are simple-minded.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.180
Sheesh, what a boisterous girl.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.200
Yep.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.560
She’s a bit slow, but she’s very determined.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.030
You chose a pretty good one.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.190
You think so too?

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.040
We shall now begin the press conference for the preview of...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.420
...Nobuhiro-san’s first work after his comeback, the movie: Only Love.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.750
First, the opening address by the lead actor, Nobuhiro-san.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:17.680
During my hospitalization and surgery, I felt the support of many people once again.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:24.730
I’m especially grateful to the hospital staff and the concerned people who gave me encouragement.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.690
Nobuhiro seems a bit different.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.980
It’s like his smile has gotten gentler.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.070
Like he’s become a better man?

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:34.480
Yeah!

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.820
As expected, my Irie-kun is amazing!

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.740
He can even change a boy’s life.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.290
I have to watch his movie!

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.990
What’s it about?

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.500
This is the original work!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.670
Want to read it?
It’s a really wonderful love story!

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.840
Let me see.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.670
The man rushes to the side of the
troubled heroine in the dead of night.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.800
He suddenly embraces her, and gives her a passionate kiss!

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.310
Seems like something Kotoko would like.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:08.980
And then, the guy secretly prepares a present for her birthday.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:12.190
But, aren’t presents normal for birthdays?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.320
Yeah.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.980
Don’t tell me you’ve never received one before, Kotoko-san?

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.610
No way! Are you serious?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.900
You’re unloved, aren’t you, Kotoko?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.410
You’ve got it wrong! Irie-kun is easily embarrassed and shy.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.830
So, it’s not like he doesn’t love me...

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.840
What?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.880
Nothing.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.470
Then this year I’ll have a birthday just like the one in that manga!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.080
Impossible.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:41.930
Impossible, isn’t it?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.010
How can you know that for sure?!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.810
Come to think of it, your birthday is next week, isn’t it?

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.980
Yeah, September 28th.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.150
Ah, there’s no time left.
It’s even more impossible now.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.770
I’ll bet my lunch tickets on it.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.820
Yeah, me too. One week of tickets says she doesn’t make it.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.650
Hmph! What’s the big idea?!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.240
Come on, guys. You don’t have to be so mean to her.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.540
Bet on her then, Tomoko.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.540
Me?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.450
So, the bets are settled then.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.290
Wait! Why am I the only one...

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.130
I will make this birthday date a reality!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.680
Eh?! But that’s so sad!

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.600
I had my hopes riding on this event!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.140
And I was close to finishing the banner too!

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.600
In that case, can I let you handle it again this year?

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.150
No, Kotoko-chan!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:39.230
It’s true that Onii-chan only participates every year because he has to.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.990
Because he has to...?

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.450
I got it!

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.620
Don’t cut any corners and have a great birthday, just the two of you!

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.580
Mother!

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.450
Kotoko-chan!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.330
Just leave it to me!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.790
Let’s make a plan!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.620
Let’s see, first, we’ll have to nonchalantly make Onii-chan aware of your birthday!

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.590
I don’t think “nonchalantly” is possible.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.370
Irie-kun?

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.340
Onii-chan?

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.260
Do you want to celebrate it with me that badly?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.430
Well, that’s been my dream.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.720
But, I’m on duty on the 28th.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.480
No way!

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.610
So, what kind of birthday would you like?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.690
Go ahead and tell me.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.480
What? But it’s embarrassing...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.110
We get dressed up.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:28.280
You show up carrying a bouquet with the number of roses equal to my age.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.790
Then we toast with champagne and have dinner.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.960
And then you carry in the birthday cake.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:38.000
And then, and then, we spend the night together alone.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.510
I can see how passionate
you are about birthdays.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.340
I’ll get someone to cover for me.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:46.840
Really?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.010
Yeah.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.100
Really really?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:49.550
Yeah.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.940
Good for you, Kotoko-chan.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.540
Irie-kun, it’s today. You remembered, right?

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.160
Yeah.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.330
7 o’clock at the lobby
of The Royal Hotel, okay?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.370
Even though it pains me to do so,

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.550
I’m handing over the celebration of
Kotoko-chan’s birthday party to you.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:24.050
Wait, Onii-chan. Did you bring a fresh change of clothes?

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.510
You’re not going to show up at night wearing this, are you?

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:30.350
Ah, Irie-kun. You don’t have to come with the bouquet of roses, okay?

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.010
What are you saying, Kotoko-chan?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.430
Make him get the bouquet ready!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.180
Give me a break!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.150
Okay.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.740
Well then, everyone. Have a nice day!

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.570
She’s in a merry mood.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.410
She really is having a birthday date.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.790
Are there any nice guys out there for us too?

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.000
Really...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.920
What is it?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.760
I win.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.090
Fine, fine.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.260
I know.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.100
Isn’t this Kotoko’s phone?

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.390
You’re right.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:19.690
I see. A date with your husband, right?

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.560
Yes, with my husband.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.110
That’s nice. How romantic.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.860
Yes, very romantic.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.490
I’m short on time. Can you please hurry?

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:29.700
Just leave it to me.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.620
I’ll doll you up in a jiffy!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:33.870
Please!

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.410
Is this a real hairstyle?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.750
Hey, Mom, she looks like a horse!

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.920
Hey, it’s rude to point!

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.170
I get the feeling that it isn’t...

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.720
Look at the time!

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:52.680
What was that?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.390
Is he alive?

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.560
Are you all right?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.980
The ambulance! Call for an ambulance!

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.600
Someone! Call the police!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.770
Are you all right?

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.030
Has someone called for an ambulance?

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:10.030
I just called for one, but the traffic around here is heavy.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.320
It hurts...

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.870
I’m a nurse.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.200
Stay calm.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.490
The ambulance will be here soon.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.540
Head angle for breathing set.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.750
Pulse: 140 bpm.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.750
First things first; I’ve got to stop the bleeding.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.010
My leg...

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.090
Leg?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.880
It might be fractured.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:36.760
Does anyone have something
I can use as a splint?

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:40.560
Fracture of the femur.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.350
I stopped the bleeding and gave basic first-aid treatment.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.020
His pulse is 140 bpm.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.690
And he’s fully conscious.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.030
Okay, got it.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:51.280
We were lucky to have a nurse on scene.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:52.820
Really?

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.700
The patient is ready.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:56.780
Understood.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.160
Now, please get on.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.830
I have to meet someone... Hey!

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.540
Why?!

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:11.010
Thank you so much.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.630
Not at all. I just did what anyone would do.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.760
Goodbye.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.850
Is there anyway we can thank you?

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.220
No, that’s not necessary.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.600
You saved his life.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.470
Really.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.350
It’s all because of you.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.060
Yes, goodbye.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.060
Thank you very much.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.190
Driver, The Royal Hotel.
Super ultra express fast, please!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:32.940
Yes!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.740
Eh? Why isn’t it here?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.080
It’s really not here.
Where did my phone go?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.960
Miss, we won’t get anywhere in this traffic.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.380
If you’re in a hurry,
then the train would be faster.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.920
Oh no! Look at the time!

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.090
I’m getting off!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.800
Wait for me, Irie-kun!

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.410
Irie-kun is going to go home!

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.050
What’s wrong with that girl?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.010
Is she injured?

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.270
Incredible.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.180
She’s all disheveled.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.510
Miss, are you all right?

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:55.110
No way... After I got all dressed up for the occasion too...

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.990
This was supposed to be the first time Irie-kun celebrated with me.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.160
But look at how it turned out.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.500
I...

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:06.120
Excuse me. For now, please come this way.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:10.460
How am I supposed to face Irie-kun looking like this?

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:13.040
Mother... Moto-chan...

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.090
Everyone, forgive me.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:24.060
I thought that was your blood... Don’t scare me like that.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.060
Irie-kun?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.190
Irie-kun!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:33.030
A lot of things happened,
and I couldn’t get here!

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.530
I wanted to call, but I lost my phone.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:40.530
And I thought that you might have gone home already.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.750
But, I couldn’t just give up.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.210
Then...

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:50.460
I knew you would come even if it killed you.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.300
I couldn’t possibly go home even if I wanted to.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.210
Irie-kun...

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.590
But, you really look like something else.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:01.810
I’m sorry. We can’t go anywhere because I’m looking like this.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:05.390
Yeah, there aren’t any stores open around this time either.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.600
Hi, you over there!

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:11.720
This bag belongs to you, right?

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:16.990
Here, take it, Onii-san.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.360
Oh, it’s time for my flight.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.490
I’m going back to my country.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:22.910
Goodbye!

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:25.540
I wish you two happiness!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.670
24, 25, 26!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.460
The exact number of roses as my age!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.090
Cake and champagne too!

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.510
Come on, let’s eat!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.720
Sheesh... what was my mother thinking?

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:50.400
But, I’m really happy.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.220
Can there be a luckier bride?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:57.190
Happy birthday, Kotoko.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.820
Irie-kun.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.620
What do you want as a present?

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.490
Well...

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.830
I’d like you to tell me that you love me.

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:13.330
No, that’s not it!
Let me think of something else.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.510
Kotoko, I love you.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.230
I love you too.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.320
So much time has passed since we first met.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:41.780
And yet, why does my heart
still beat so quickly?

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.870
Why do I love him so much?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:01.630
Will Irie-kun continue to love me too?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:12.480
Will there be things that will make my heart race from time to time?

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.610
It’d be great if that were so.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.160
Irie-san, what are you smiling about?

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.210
I’m so glad you asked!

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.580
You see, during my birthday, Irie-kun...

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.880
She said it.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.540
This is gonna be long.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:41.340
Irie-kun secretly bought this ring for me.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:43.800
Furthermore, it fits perfectly!

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.390
As expected from a genius.

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:48.680
He even knew that my birthstone was a sapphire.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.060
Irie-san.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.180
Irie Kotoko-san!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.690
Head nurse?

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:56.270
I’m glad you’re as cheerful as ever.

00:15:56.770 --> 00:16:02.110
But, the internal medicine ward is lacking staff because a lot nurses have taken leave.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.820
Good thing you’re here.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:05.820
I’d like you to go there.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:06.780
Yes.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.420
Oh, Irie-kun?
Why are you in Internal Medicine?

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.910
They were lacking staff.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.920
What a wonderful coincidence!

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:22.710
Then, as a married couple, let’s do our best!

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.130
Excuse me, help here!

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.510
I told you, I’m fine!

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.420
That voice.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.010
Sudou-san?

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.140
Oh, Irie!

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:31.390
Irie-kun?

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:36.020
Sudou-sempai and Matsumoto-san?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.900
Why are you two here?

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.860
Matsumoto suddenly collapsed.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.820
Collapsed?

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.740
It’s no big deal.

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.530
I was just feeling a little anemic.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.740
And I twisted my ankle a little.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:51.240
Luckily, I happened to be with her by chance.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.080
What do you mean by chance?

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.210
You’re always around, telling me to buy business vehicles and such.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:58.210
You’re such a nuisance.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:00.790
Anyway, Irie. Please take a look at her.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:04.590
Sure thing. Sprains are handled by the orthopedic department.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.180
You sure never change, Sudou-sempai.

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.300
Whatever, just show us the way.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.260
Okay. This way please–

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:18.390
Irie-san! How many times
do I have to tell you?!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.270
It never changes, does it?

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:42.700
Finally, some time to myself.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:47.220
But this department sure is busy...

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.000
Irie-kun!

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.230
Careful.

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:00.400
Don’t you have a fever?

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.770
I guess I am a bit feverish.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:06.190
Have you eaten?

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.990
No, I haven’t.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:11.240
I wasn’t hungry and it’s been so busy too.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:15.240
Aww, don’t, Irie-kun.
Are you worrying about me?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.410
It’s love, isn’t it? Love for your beloved wife, isn’t it?

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.120
I’m glad you’re well.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.960
Dr. Irie! Emergency!

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:26.130
We have a five-year old child who’s fading in and out of consciousness!

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.460
Understood. I’m going there now.

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:37.850
Doctor, how’s Takashi?

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.430
There’s some vomit lodged inside his throat.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.650
Kotoko, prepare the tube.

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:43.560
Right away!

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:47.400
Ma’am, I’m going to have to insert a tube into your son’s throat...

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.940
...and suck out the vomit
lodged in his esophagus.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.950
Dr. Irie, it’s ready!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:58.790
Kotoko, he might move violently from the pain, so hold him down.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:18:59.540
Right.

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.330
Oh dear! Pain?

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:07.550
It’ll be fine. Dr. Irie is the finest suction expert in all of Japan.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.300
I see. Please.

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:12.840
Takashi, be strong!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.930
Mama is here with you.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.430
Okay, Takashi-kun. Open wide.

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:18.890
It’ll be over soon.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:24.100
Kotoko, hold him down properly!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.270
Yes!

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:28.390
What are you doing?!
You’re not holding him down!

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:29.730
Yes!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:33.740
Takashi!

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:37.080
Be strong, Takashi!

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.740
It’s okay! Mama is here.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.620
Mama is here, so it’ll be fine.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.500
Okay, it’s fine now.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.040
Takashi!

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.540
You did well.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.630
Good boy!

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.050
Mama!

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:57.000
Thank you very much.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.060
Good boy, Takashi-kun.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:04.930
It’s all thanks to the kind-hearted nurse and Japan’s best suction doctor.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:08.440
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:10.810
You don’t have to...

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.320
Bye-bye.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.990
Isn’t that nice?

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:21.120
That was the first time you were ever praised as a nurse, wasn’t it?

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.910
Of course not! How rude!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.830
But, looks like I’m the best suction doctor in Japan.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.590
But, I’m so happy.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.220
Mothers are truly amazing, aren’t they?

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.970
Their power to protect their children is really something else!

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:40.930
It sure is.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.850
Dr. Irie!

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:44.930
We have another emergency!

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.520
What a day.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:50.020
All right! Then, we’ll make one more effort!

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.280
I’m home.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:20:59.740
Good job.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.410
Looks like things have been rough.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:04.620
Mother, sorry about this.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:08.080
Kotoko-chan, your face is a little flushed.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.460
Are you all right?

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.670
I might be a bit feverish.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.380
Isn’t it a cold?

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:17.130
Shouldn’t you take some medicine?

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.380
Yeah.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.170
No, hold the medicine.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:22.720
Why?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.220
Kotoko, aren’t...

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.440
...you pregnant?

00:23:06.490 --> 00:23:08.030
Aihara-san is pregnant?!

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:10.200
Well done Irie, you rascal!

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.620
One day, Matsumoto and I will too.

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:14.370
Stop planning such strange things!

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:18.420
Besides, I like guys who are capable workers.

00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:19.500
Really?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.710
I see. All right then!

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:23.300
Hey, what’s with you?

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:25.380
I’m gonna do it!

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:27.840
Next time on Itazura na Kiss:

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:29.880
You, go around, me.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.640
I’m definitely gonna be happy.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:33.270
Hold it!
